  "notes": "{休|やす}める is an ichidan verb meaning to rest or give rest to something.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{休|やす}む→休む：00606_yasumu⟧ (intransitive - to rest, take a break)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{体|からだ}→体：00784_karada⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{休|やす}める: to rest one's body\n- ⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{休|やす}める: to rest one's eyes\n- ⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{休|やす}める: to ease one's mind\n- ⟦{足|あし}→足：00575_ashi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{休|やす}める: to rest one's feet\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ⟦{羽|はね}→羽：03696_hane⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{休|やす}める: to take a breather (lit. rest one's wings)\n- ⟦{手|て}→手：00569_te⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{休|やす}める: to stop working temporarily\n\nUSAGE:\nUsed when giving rest to a specific body part or the body as a whole, as opposed to ⟦{休|やす}む→休む：00606_yasumu⟧ which is more general (to take a day off, to rest).",
